fresh outta the dryer.

4
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:06.240
Ooh, I do love that.

5
00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:07.390
Ooh, the best!
Oh!

6
00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:09.173
Feetsies are cold.

7
00:00:09.173 --> 00:00:10.880
Boo, now they're warm.

8
00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:13.770
And human warm sock, Rossy Ross Matthews.

9
00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:14.950
Yeah, well, thank you so much.

10
00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:15.783
(audience cheers)

11
00:00:15.783 --> 00:00:19.257
Hi, hi, hi!

12
00:00:19.257 --> 00:00:20.260
(Drew chuckles)

13
00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:23.420
Speaking of coming out, warm from something.

14
00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:24.680
Our first story

15
00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:26.060
is kind of that.
(Ross titters)

16
00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:28.140
Great transition (laughs).

17
00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:30.470
What does Stephen King make for dinner?

18
00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:31.303
Great question.

19
00:00:31.303 --> 00:00:33.790
Well, we've got the answer and it's chilling

20
00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:36.000
in today's Food News.

21
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.660
Num, num, num.
Num, num, num, aw.

22
00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:38.545
Okay.

23
00:00:38.545 --> 00:00:39.503
(audience cheers)

24
00:00:39.503 --> 00:00:40.852
Yeah.

25
00:00:40.852 --> 00:00:41.880
(audience cheers)

26
00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.823
So the New York Post reports
This is frightening.

27
00:00:43.823 --> 00:00:46.970
that Stephen King is horrifying fans yet again

28
00:00:46.970 --> 00:00:49.355
but this time with microwaved fish.

29
00:00:49.355 --> 00:00:50.188
(Ross chuckles)

30
00:00:50.188 --> 00:00:52.140
He posted this recipe on Twitter.

31
00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:54.890
For a man who's written 1000s of pages,

32
00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:57.720 line:15%
it's so simple, it's actually scary.

33
00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:01.230 line:15%
Get a nice salmon filet, not too big.

34
00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:03.880 line:15%
Puts some olive oil and lemon juice on it.

35
00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:05.810 line:15%
Wrap it in damp paper towels.

36
00:01:05.810 --> 00:01:08.460 line:15%
Nuke it in the microwave for three minutes.

37
00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:09.293 line:15%
Mm-mm.
Eat it.

38
00:01:09.293 --> 00:01:10.380 line:15%
Mm-mm, mm-mm!

39
00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:12.950 line:15%
I'm sorry for, what do you have?

40
00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:15.404 line:15%
Oh God, no, you do not.

41
00:01:15.404 --> 00:01:16.237 line:15%
(audience laughs)

42
00:01:16.237 --> 00:01:17.971 line:15%
(audience cheers)

43
00:01:17.971 --> 00:01:20.200 line:15%
It's not carbs!

44
00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:21.033
Okay.

45
00:01:21.033 --> 00:01:22.250
It's not carbs, Rossy.

46
00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:26.360
I feel so honored that I'm not shoving a bagel

47
00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:27.200
or a pizza,
Not a thing.

48
00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:28.410
or a Fettuccine Alfredo

49
00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:29.640
down your throat.
It's always a croissant

50
00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:31.000
or something here.

51
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:34.180
I will say, I can't believe he microwaves his fish.

52
00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:35.820
For a man who wrote Fire Starter,

53
00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:37.556
you can't light a flame, hello!

54
00:01:37.556 --> 00:01:39.260
(audience laughs)

55
00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:41.610
Alright, so, we're both gonna try this?

56
00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:42.765
You're gonna try it.

57
00:01:42.765 --> 00:01:44.274
(audience laughs)
(Ross laughs)

58
00:01:44.274 --> 00:01:45.107
(Drew chuckles)

59
00:01:45.107 --> 00:01:46.730
All right, I'm gonna do a little lemon,

60
00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:47.563
just like you said.

61
00:01:47.563 --> 00:01:49.730
I have to say, it does look really nice.

62
00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:50.900
It does.
I got scared.

63
00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:51.817
And I was like,

64
00:01:51.817 --> 00:01:53.380
"I'll let Ross try it."
God!

65
00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:54.213
Okay.
And then now I'm looking

66
00:01:54.213 --> 00:01:55.690
at it and I'm thinking I made a mistake.

67
00:01:55.690 --> 00:01:56.830
All right, I'll tell you.

68
00:01:56.830 --> 00:01:58.430
I'm not afraid of a little microwave.

69
00:01:58.430 --> 00:01:59.467
All right, ready?

70
00:01:59.467 --> 00:02:02.412
(man chuckles)

71
00:02:02.412 --> 00:02:03.785
(audience laughs)

72
00:02:03.785 --> 00:02:05.560
Pretty cool!

73
00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:08.602
Stephen King, there's nothing fishy going on here.

74
00:02:08.602 --> 00:02:09.490
(audience laughs)

75
00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:12.010
Actually, it's flaky, it works.

76
00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:13.791
What, that's like?

77
00:02:13.791 --> 00:02:17.187
(audience cheers)

78
00:02:17.187 --> 00:02:20.690
That's like a twist I didn't see coming.

79
00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:22.920
It's actually delicious, here Drew.

80
00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:25.550
(audience laughs)

81
00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:30.550
Well, I'll tell you a story

82
00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:31.453
about Stephen King

83
00:02:31.453 --> 00:02:32.880
instead of eating the salmon.

84
00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:33.750
Do you wanna just smell it?

85
00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:34.912
Nope.
Understood.

86
00:02:34.912 --> 00:02:36.479
(audience laughs)

87
00:02:36.479 --> 00:02:37.312
(Ross laughs)

88
00:02:37.312 --> 00:02:39.130
Stephen King, I went to stay at his house

89
00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:40.721
because I did Fire Starter with him.

90
00:02:40.721 --> 00:02:42.480
Of course.
And then I did this movie

91
00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:43.313
Cat's Eye with him

92
00:02:43.313 --> 00:02:44.290
which was really just stories

93
00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:46.050
taken from his book Night Shift.

94
00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:48.170
And so I got to go stay up at his house

95
00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:49.800
in Maine when I was a kid.

96
00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:53.963
And it was the most joyful weekend of my life.

97
00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:59.100
They had a house that was just so filled with soul

98
00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:01.430
and his wife, Tabitha and their kids.

99
00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:03.500
And he made pancakes in the kitchen

100
00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:07.060
and then his office was upstairs in the attic

101
00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:11.038
and he had a pet scorpion named Boris.

102
00:03:11.038 --> 00:03:12.370
(audience laughs)

103
00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:14.080
So, no salmon for me,

104
00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:17.510
but that fun story is what I will offer

105
00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:18.769
about Stephen King.

106
00:03:18.769 --> 00:03:19.602
(audience claps)

107
00:03:19.602 --> 00:03:22.000
I love Stephen King so much.

108
00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.470
And you know, if he wants to add salmon

109
00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.730
to that illustrious resume,

110
00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:28.930
microwave salmon, so be it.

111
00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:29.866
Yeah.

112
00:03:29.866 --> 00:03:32.699
(audience cheers)

113
00:03:33.926 --> 00:03:34.759
(Ross chuckles)

114
00:03:34.759 --> 00:03:36.950
You know why I love having a conversation with you?

115
00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:37.820
Why?
Because it can go

116
00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:38.790
from microwave salmon

117
00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:39.740
to, "That one time

118
00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:42.020
I met Stephen King's scorpion, Boris."

119
00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:43.840
You know, you just strap on,

120
00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:45.850
you never know where it's gonna take you.

121
00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:47.333
Hell that's...
So I didn't see that coming.

122
00:03:47.333 --> 00:03:49.916 line:15%
(upbeat music)

